From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A7om <hatter6822@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hw/timer/bcm2835_systmr: Stop comparators and lower
 interrupts on reset

Reset clears the registers but leaves each comparator's QEMUTimer armed
and its interrupt line as it was. After a system reset an old compare
value can therefore still fire and set a status bit in the fresh
CTRL_STATUS, and an interrupt raised before the reset stays asserted
with no status bit left for the guest to acknowledge.

Cancel the timers and lower the lines along with the register reset.
While here, drop the stale claim that the comparators are not
implemented.
---
 hw/timer/bcm2835_systmr.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/timer/bcm2835_systmr.c b/hw/timer/bcm2835_systmr.c
index 06a919b..17a0e7d 100644
--- a/hw/timer/bcm2835_systmr.c
+++ b/hw/timer/bcm2835_systmr.c
@@ -8,8 +8,8 @@
  * Datasheet: BCM2835 ARM Peripherals (C6357-M-1398)
  * https://www.raspberrypi.org/app/uploads/2012/02/BCM2835-ARM-Peripherals.pdf
  *
- * Only the free running 64-bit counter is implemented.
- * The 4 COMPARE registers and the interruption are not implemented.
+ * A free running 64-bit counter at 1 MHz and four 32-bit comparators, each
+ * raising its own interrupt when the low word of the counter matches it.
  */
 
 #include "qemu/osdep.h"
@@ -122,6 +122,10 @@ static void bcm2835_systmr_reset(DeviceState *dev)
 {
     BCM2835SystemTimerState *s = BCM2835_SYSTIMER(dev);
 
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(s->tmr); i++) {
+        timer_del(&s->tmr[i].timer);
+        qemu_set_irq(s->tmr[i].irq, 0);
+    }
     memset(&s->reg, 0, sizeof(s->reg));
 }
 
